Overview
This document specifies how the ambiguity document reviewer and spell checker integrate with GitHub Actions via permission request hooks. The hook accepts input payloads from workflow_dispatch events and validates them before executing the review pipeline.

The system has two primary components:

Component	Purpose
Ambiguity Document Reviewer	Detects unclear or ambiguous statements in documentation that could cause misinterpretation
Spell Checker	Validates spelling against the author allowlist and project dictionaries
Both components share a unified input payload schema and permission model.

Permission Request Hook Schema
Hook Registration
The hook registers as a GitHub App webhook listener for workflow_dispatch and repository_dispatch events.

# .github/workflows/ambiguity-review.yml
name: Ambiguity Review and Spell Check

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      # See full schema below
      blacme:
        description: 'Blame attribution mode'
        required: true
        default: 'auto'
      document_paths:
        description: 'Glob patterns for documents to review'
        required: false
        default: '**/*.md'
      spell_check_level:
        description: 'Spell check severity'
        required: false
        default: 'suggest'
      language_override:
        description: 'Locale override (e.g., en-US, es)'
        required: false
        default: ''
      strict_mode:
        description: 'Fail on any detected issue'
        required: false
        type: boolean
        default: false
  repository_dispatch:
    types: [ambiguity-review-trigger]

permissions:
  contents: read
  pull-requests: write
  actions: read

jobs:
  review:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0
          
      - name: Validate inputs
        id: validate
        run: |
          python scripts/validate_hook_inputs.py \
            --blacme "${{ inputs.blacme }}" \
            --paths "${{ inputs.document_paths }}" \
            --level "${{ inputs.spell_check_level }}"
          
      - name: Run ambiguity review
        id: ambiguity
        run: |
          npx ambiguity-review \
            --input "${{ github.event.inputs.document_paths }}" \
            --output reports/ambiguity-report.json
            
      - name: Run spell check
        id: spellcheck
        run: |
          npx cspell "${{ github.event.inputs.document_paths }}" \
            --config cspell.json \
            --no-progress
            
      - name: Post review comment
        if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'
        run: |
          npx ambiguity-review post-comment \
            --report reports/ambiguity-report.json \
            --pr ${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}
