## Multilingual support and per-file overrides

### Locale-aware checking

Different parts of a repository may be written in different languages. The extension supports per-file locale configuration using the `languageSettings` mechanism, which separates **spoken language** (locale) from **programming language** (file type).

```json
{
  "language": "en",
  "languageSettings": [
    {
      "languageId": "",
      "locale": "en",
      "description": "Default for English content"
    },
    {
      "languageId": "python,javascript",
      "locale": "es",
      "dictionaries": ["es"]
    },
    {
      "languageId": "markdown",
      "locale": "de",
      "dictionaries": ["de-de"]
    },
    {
      "languageId": "latex",
      "locale": "fr",
      "dictionaries": ["fr-fr"]
    }
  ]
}
```

| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `languageId` | Programming language (file type): `python`, `markdown`, `latex`, etc. Use `""` to match all file types. |
| `locale` | Spoken language locale: `en-US`, `de-AT`, `zh-CN`. Use `""` to match all locales. |
| `dictionaries` | Which dictionaries to enable for this combination. |

Multiple locales can be specified: `"locale": "en, en-US"` matches both US and generic English.

### File-type overrides

For files that don't match standard extensions, force a specific treatment:

```json
{
  "overrides": [
    {
      "filename": "/.xyz",
      "languageId": "javascript"
    },
    {
      "filename": "/docs/**/*.txt",
      "languageId": "markdown",
      "dictionaries": ["en-gb"]
    },
    {
      "filename": "/tests/**/*.ts",
      "dictionaries": ["en-us", "lorem-ipsum"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Available language dictionaries

CSpell maintains separate dictionaries for dozens of spoken and programming languages. Some examples:

| Locale | Dictionary ID | File types |
|---|---|---|
| English (US) | `en-us` | All |
| English (GB) | `en-gb` | All |
| Spanish | `es-es` | All |
| French | `fr-fr` | All |
| German | `de-de` | All |
| Chinese | `zh` | All |
| Portuguese (BR) | `pt-br` | All |
| Japanese | `ja` | All |
| Python | `python` | `.py` files |
| JavaScript | `javascript` | `.js`, `.jsx` |
| TypeScript | `typescript` | `.ts`, `.tsx` |
| Markdown | `markdown` | `.md` |
| Rust | `rust` | `.rs` |
| Go | `go` | `.go` |

See [cspell-dicts](https://github.com/streetsidesoftware/cspell-dicts) for the full catalog.

