## Permissions and data handling

| Concern | Position |
|---|---|
| Scopes requested | `contents: read`, `metadata: read`; `pull-requests: write` only for the report comment |
| Data sent off-platform | None. Dictionary generation and checking run locally or in your runner |
| Personal data | Names and email addresses already exist in public git history; the extension reads them, it does not enrich them |
| Retention | Generated dictionaries live in the repository and are subject to your own retention policy |
| Third-party models | No AI model is invoked. The checker is a deterministic dictionary lookup |

> [!WARNING]
> Because the generated dictionary contains contributor names and email-derived handles, treat `.github/author-names.txt` as you would any other file containing personal data. If your project strips authorship from public history, do not commit the generated file — generate it in CI and cache it as an ephemeral artifact instead.

